Note on the proving toolchain
-----------------------------

`@orb/payment-circuit` depends on snarkjs and circomlibjs, and its build step
uses the circom compiler. Those are GPL-3.0. That package is therefore the one
piece of this repository whose distribution terms are not simply Apache-2.0,
and anyone redistributing it should take their own advice on the combination.

@orb/hyperliquid carries two MIT dependencies (@noble/curves, @noble/hashes)
for signing, which combine with Apache-2.0 without qualification.

@orb/journal, @orb/payment-policy and @orb/trade-executor have no third-party
runtime dependencies at all. That was not an accident: the engine that decides
whether money moves was kept dependency-free so it could run anywhere, offline,
with nothing installed -- and a clean licensing position is a welcome side
effect of the same decision.
